Ideal gas equation $\mathrm{PV}=\mathrm{nRT}\begin{aligned}
& \frac{P_1 V_1}{T_1}=\frac{P_2 V_2}{T_2} \\
& T_2=\frac{P_2 V_2 \times T_1}{P_1 V_1}=\frac{0.2 \times 304 \times 10^3 \times 400}{0.5 \times 203 \times 10^3} \\
& =239.6
\end{aligned}$<br/>Change in temperature $=400-239.6\begin{aligned}
& =160.4 \\
& =160 \mathrm{approx}
\end{aligned}$
